   "source": [
    "# Sprint 3 — Data Pipeline Report"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1055daac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook verifies and reports on the data pipeline built in `src/data/`\n",
    "for Sprint 3 (`dataset.py`, `transforms.py`, `dataloader.py`, `label_map.py`,\n",
    "`loaders.py`). No pipeline code is written here — this notebook only\n",
    "imports from `src`, runs it against both datasets (mushroom, flower), and\n",
    "reports the results. Any bug found here gets fixed in `src/`, not here.\n",
    "\n",
    "Research question: can a single, reusable, configuration-driven data\n",
    "pipeline serve both datasets without dataset-specific code paths?\n",
    "\n",
    "What we check:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Dataset sanity: `dataset[0]` shape and value range\n",
    "- Batch shape sanity: `next(iter(loader))`\n",
    "- Batch visualization (labels + augmented images)\n",
    "- Augmentation on/off comparison (does augmentation actually do something?)\n",
    "- A mini benchmark: image size, batch size, augmentation on/off vs load time"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "758e249d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
