   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Dataset Sanity Check\n",
    "\n",
    "`dataset[0]` should return a `(3, image_size, image_size)` tensor. We also\n",
    "print the value range: after `Normalize` with ImageNet mean/std, this should\n",
    "sit roughly in `[-2.1, 2.6]` — if it doesn't (e.g. it's still `[0, 1]`),\n",
    "`Normalize` silently isn't being applied, which is exactly the kind of bug\n",
    "that trains a model quietly worse without throwing an error."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "62c164b5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-09T09:19:28.689375Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-09T09:19:28.689375Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-09T09:19:28.759300Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-09T09:19:28.759300Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Mushroom: shape=(3, 224, 224), dtype=torch.float32, range=(-2.015, 2.553), label_index=98\n",
